54.620218,"lo":-5.869956,"d":1934,"w":"https://www.belfastcityairport.com/","ph":"+44 28 90939093","wp":"en:George Best Belfast City Airport","wifi":1,"ds":"Belfast City Airport, formally George Best Belfast City Airport (IATA: BHD, ICAO: EGAC), is an international airport in Belfast, Northern Ireland. Situated in County Down, it is adjacent to the Belfast Harbour and is three miles (five kilometres) from Belfast City Centre. It shares the site with the Spirit AeroSystems (formerly Short Brothers/Bombardier) aircraft manufacturing facility.","wpu":"Belfast City Airport","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/George_Best_Belfast_City_Airport_-_geograph.org.uk_-_714574.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"McKenzies Chemist","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":54.612014,"lo":-5.926837,"d":1942},{"n":"Business Hub - Departures Lounge","g":"essentials","k":"wifi","la":54.614592,"lo":-5.871063,"d":1957,"wifi":1},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":54.614504,"lo":-5.870762,"d":1979},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":54.614862,"lo":-5.870436,"d":1987},{"n":"RBS","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":54.609982,"lo":-5.926585,"d":2042},{"n":"Currency exchange","g":"essentials","k":"bureau_de_change","la":54.609899,"lo":-5.926695,"d":2053},{"n":"Busby's Chemist","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":54.612485,"lo":-5.929562,"d":2078},{"n":"Yorkgate Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":54.609688,"lo":-5.926972,"d":2081,"h":"Mo-Sa 08:00-20:00; Su 10:00-16:00","w":"https://www.postoffice.co.uk/branch-finder/2507048/yorkgate-shopping-centre"},{"n":"Tesco","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":54.609544,"lo":-5.926954,"d":2089,"h":"Mo-Sa 08:00-21:00; Su 13:00-18:00","w":"https://www.tesco.com/store-locator/belfast/100-150-york-st","ph":"+44 345 677 9754"},{"n":"Stena Line Victoria Terminal 4","g":"essentials","k":"ferry_terminal","la":54.635601,"lo":-5.881583,"d":2101,"wp":"en:Stena Line","wifi":1,"ds":"Stena Line is a Swedish shipping line company and one of the world's largest ferry operators. It services Denmark, France, Germany, the United Kingdom, Ireland, Latvia, the Netherlands, Poland, Finland and Sweden. Stena Line is a major unit of Stena AB, itself a part of the Stena Sphere.","wpu":"Stena Line","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Stena_line_logo.svg/960px-Stena_line_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sydenham Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":54.604027,"lo":-5.881163,"d":2150,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-18:00; Sa 09:00-13:00","w":"https://www.postoffice.co.uk/branch-finder/4097041/sydenham"},{"n":"Strandburn Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":54.604015,"lo":-5.881109,"d":2153},{"n":"Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":54.599061,"lo":-5.900751,"d":2328},{"n":"Newtownards Road Post Office","g":"essentials","k":"post_office","la":54.598859,"lo":-5.8973,"d":2357,"h":"Mo 08:00-17:30; Tu-Sa 09:00-17:30","w":"https://www.postoffice.co.uk/branch-finder/2647044/newtownards-road"},{"n":"Belfast Harbour","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.617778,"lo":-5.901667,"d":269,"ds":"Belfast Harbour is a major maritime hub in Belfast, Northern Ireland, handling 67% of Northern Ireland's seaborne trade and about 25% of the maritime trade of the entire island of Ireland. It is a vital gateway for raw materials, exports and consumer goods, and is also Northern Ireland's leading logistics and distribution hub.","wpu":"Belfast Harbour","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Belfast_Container_Terminal%2C_April_2019.jpg/960px-Belfast_Container_Terminal%2C_April_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"RFA Fort Victoria bombing","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.618717,"lo":-5.895067,"d":348,"ds":"The bombing of RFA Fort Victoria took place on 6 September 1990, when a unit of the Provisional Irish Republican Army (IRA) planted two bombs aboard the Royal Fleet Auxiliary replenishment ship at Harland & Wolff shipyard in Belfast, Northern Ireland, where the vessel had been launched four months before. One of them exploded in the engine room, causing flooding and serious damage.","wpu":"RFA Fort Victoria bombing","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ed/FTVMalaga.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Catalyst (science park)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.608,"lo":-5.903,"d":1348,"ds":"Catalyst, formerly known as the Northern Ireland Science Park, was established in March 1999 to create a self-sustaining, internationally recognised, knowledge-based science park in Northern Ireland offering a commercial and research driven centre for knowledge-based industries.","wpu":"Catalyst (science park)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Catalyst_.jpg/960px-Catalyst_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Victoria Park, Belfast","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.6073,"lo":-5.8886,"d":1591,"ds":"Victoria Park was opened in 1906 in the Connswater area of Belfast. Belfast Harbour Commissioners investigated the idea in 1854, however the land was very marshy and needed draining near Belfast Lough. It was landscaped by Charles McKimm, who also built the Tropical Ravine in Botanic Gardens.","wpu":"Victoria Park, Belfast","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Victoria_Park_-_geograph.org.uk_-_119498.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Alexandra Park, Belfast","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.618,"lo":-5.932,"d":2072,"ds":"Alexandra Park is a Victorian park situated in north Belfast. It is named after Princess Alexandra of Saxe-Coburg and Gotha and was opened in 1888. As is typical for parks of the period, it has a formal layout that includes tree lined avenues.","wpu":"Alexandra Park, Belfast","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Alexandra_Park_Belfast.JPG/960px-Alexandra_Park_Belfast.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Obel Tower","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.602,"lo":-5.922,"d":2452,"ds":"The Obel Tower is a highrise building in Belfast, Northern Ireland, located on Donegall Quay on the River Lagan beside the Lagan Weir. Measuring 85 metres (279 ft) in height, the tower is the tallest storeyed building in Ireland, dominating the Belfast skyline. On completion it overtook the previous tallest building in Belfast and Northern Ireland, Windsor House (80 m).","wpu":"Obel Tower","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c5/Belfast%27s_Obel_Tower_overlooking_the_River_Lagan._-_geograph.org.uk_-_3157717.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Lagan Weir","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.60086,"lo":-5.92,"d":2487,"ds":"The Lagan Weir, in Belfast, Northern Ireland, crosses the River Lagan between the Queen Elizabeth Bridge and the M3 cross-harbour bridge. Prior to the building of the weir, the river would be subject to tidal fluctuations, and low tide would expose mudflats, which were unsightly and emitted a strong odour, particularly in the summer months.","wpu":"Lagan Weir","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Queen%27s_Quay_and_Lagan_Weir%2C_Belfast%2C_April_2010.JPG/960px-Queen%27s_Quay_and_Lagan_Weir%2C_Belfast%2C_April_2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St Mark's Church, Dundela","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":54.603,"lo":-5.8747,"d":2495,"ds":"St Mark's Church, Dundela, is a Grade A listed parish church of the Church of Ireland located in the Sydenham area of Belfast, Northern Ireland.","wpu":"St Mark's Church, Dundela","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/af/St_Mark%27s_Church%2C_Dundela%2C_Belfast_-_geograph.org.uk_-_901404.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Belfast ( BEL-fast, , -⁠fahst; from Irish: Béal Feirste [bʲeːlˠ ˈfʲɛɾˠ(ə)ʃtʲə]) is the capital, largest city and main port of Northern Ireland. It stands on the banks of the river Lagan, and is connected to the open sea through Belfast Lough and the North Channel. The city is the most populous in Northern Ireland and the second-largest, after Dublin, on the island of Ireland, with a recorded population in 2021 of 345,418 and of 704,406 for the greater metropolitan area.","wpu":"Belfast","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Belfast_Skyline_City_Quays.png/960px-Belfast_Skyline_City_Quays.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}